 "derivation": "Ottoman Turkish تلبند tülbend / dülbend is a straight borrowing of Classical Persian dulband, with Turkish front-vowel harmony (u > ü) and the usual d- ~ t- fluctuation; in Turkish the sense narrowed from 'turban' to 'the muslin/gauze it is wound from', which is all modern Turkish tülbent means. Skeat s.v. TURBAN: 'Turk. tulbend, vulgar form of dulband, a turban. - Pers. dulband, a turban.' Lokotsch no.544 gives the same: pers. dulband > tk. tülbend 'Musseline, Kopftuch daraus', tülbent 'Brautschleier', turban.",
