 "derivation": "Empty pass-through box; the French link is turbant (15c.), modern turban. The standard authorities insert an Italian stage that the chart's arrow Turkish -> French leaves out: Etymonline 'from French turbant (15c.), from Italian turbante (Old Italian tolipante), from Turkish tülbent'; likewise Skeat, Klein and Lokotsch 544 (tk. > it. turbante, frz. turban). The l > r dissimilation is placed by Etymonline in Portuguese India rather than in Turkish or French.",
